## Output contract

Print exactly one JSON object on stdout, and nothing after it. Its shape:

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "k1",
      "type": "{{.ExampleType}}",
      "title": "Short label",
{{- if eq .ExampleType "persona"}}
      "persona": {"description": "...", "goals": ["..."], "capabilities": ["..."]},
{{- else}}
      "requirement": {"statement": "...", "kind": "business-rule", "rationale": "", "personas": []},
{{- end}}
      "support": ["A.i1", "B.i2"],
      "disagreements": [
        {
          "summary": "What the interpretations disagree on.",
          "positions": [
            {"statement": "First view.", "support": ["A.i1"]},
            {"statement": "Second view.", "support": ["B.i2"]}
          ]
        }
      ],
      "uncertainties": ["Why part of this item is doubtful."],
      "questions": ["Something a human should settle."]
    }
  ]
}
```

Rules, checked by Raun without exception:

- Every interpretation id of every report appears in the `support` of exactly one item, whose `type` matches the interpretation's type.
- A disagreement has at least two positions. Each position's `support` lists interpretations of the item's own `support`; one interpretation backs at most one position.
- Each item carries exactly the content block of its `type`. Item ids are short and unique (`k1`, `k2`…).
- There is no field for evidence: evidence comes from the analysts only. No other fields are accepted.
- `disagreements`, `uncertainties` and `questions` may be empty lists.
